# Spec Platform — Plan

> Execution phases. Each phase ships independently.

## Phase 0: Dogfood Complete (done)

- [x] SPEC.dog — product spec with screens, flows, stories
- [x] constitution.dog — 7 principles, tech constraints, governance
- [x] data-model.dog — 15 entities (Node, Edge, Task, Prediction, Vector, Event, Compile, DAG) with descriptions
- [x] COPY.dog — every CLI string, every state
- [x] DESIGN-SYSTEM.dog — tokens → primitives → components → patterns → screens
- [x] dotdog validate runs on own specs (100%)
- [x] dotdog analyze — 0 gaps
- [x] dotdog list shows spec-platform project
- [x] dotdog init scaffolds new projects
- [x] dotdog compile — typed parser, .dag v1.2 with provable token savings
- [x] MCP server live (`dotdog serve`)

## Phase 1: .dog DSL Grammar + Parser (done)

- [x] Formal grammar specification (grammar.ts — EBNF + typed AST)
- [x] Lexer: section splitter, block detection, YAML tokenizer
- [x] Parser: parse() function, text → AST
- [x] AST types: DocumentNode, SectionNode, EntityNode, RelationshipNode, etc.
- [x] `dotdog parse` command: reads .dog file, outputs AST
- [x] Compile uses typed parser (no more regex hacks)

## Phase 1.5: npm Publish + CLI (done)

- [x] npm publish: dotdog@0.3.1 on npm (latest)
- [x] 11 commands: validate, analyze, generate, simulate, compile, visualize, serve, staleness, parse, init, list
- [x] Hidden command: `dotdog woof` — ASCII Spec the dog
- [x] `dotdog compile` — .dog → .dag (v1.3: full property schemas, lifecycle, categories, token method)
- [x] .dag formal specification (format-spec-dag.dog v1.3)
- [x] `dotdog generate` — fills missing files from SPEC.dog
- [x] `dotdog analyze` — deep analysis, entity audit, gap detection
- [x] `dotdog simulate` — scenario runner (phase 1 stub)
- [x] `dotdog visualize` — Mermaid graph from .dag, --save writes .md
- [x] `dotdog staleness` — detect spec/reality drift (Phases 1-3 only)
- [x] CI publish via OIDC Trusted Publishing (Node 24)
- [x] Path resolution: tilde (~) support, path traversal guard, traverse depth cap
- [x] Auto-version from package.json
- [x] npm hygiene: homepage, bugs, engines fields; trimmed keywords; correct README
- [x] GitHub Pages — specdog.github.io/dotdog (clean light theme, dog SVG, no legs)
- [x] llms.txt — llmstxt.org spec
- [x] AGENTS.md — AI agent instructions
- [x] VS Code extension: .dog syntax highlighting
- [x] Spec the dog widget: face-only, bone in mouth, feed/pet/fetch (V/C/P keys)
- [x] Path traversal: ancestor dirs allowed (bug fix — was blocking `validate ..`)
- [x] CI smoke tests: version, help, validate, analyze, staleness, list
- [x] Fixed: compile duplicate nodes — parseSections no longer double-walks headings (#101)
- [x] Fixed: init directory layout — removed double-nesting, .dog files live in project dir (#100)
- [x] Simplified: scanners read .dog files directly from project dir (no inner `specs/`)
- [x] Project detection: only dirs with SPEC.dog are treated as projects
- [x] Fixed: section parsing — `###` headings correctly split, entity headers included (#101 follow-up)

## Phase 2: Distribution

- [x] Branch protection: 1 review required, no force push
- [x] Security: Dependabot alerts + auto-fixes enabled
- [x] VS Code extension: syntax highlighting (extensions/vscode/)
- [ ] GitHub Action: `dotdog/validate` blocks PRs with broken specs

## Phase 3: MCP Server Live (done)

- [x] `dotdog serve` — MCP server over stdio
- [x] 6 tools: getEntity, traverse, search, schema, summary, listProjects

## Phase 4: Vector Embeddings

- [ ] Parse spec sections into chunks
- [ ] Embed with all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (384 dims, local, $0)
- [ ] Store embeddings in SQLite
- [ ] Semantic search: `dotdog search "payment"` returns relevant sections
- [ ] Contradiction detection
- [ ] Staleness detection

## Phase 5: Graph Traversal Engine

- [ ] Build in-memory graph from parsed entities + relationships
- [ ] BFS hop depth audit
- [ ] Query API: traversals, state queries, critical path
- [ ] `dotdog simulate` — full engine: walk through scenario, check pre/postconditions
- [ ] Completion probability: compute from historical velocity + remaining tasks

## Phase 6: Prediction Tracking

- [ ] Predictions stored in SQLite with triggers, timeframes, confidence
- [ ] Prediction resolution: mark as correct/wrong/partially_correct
- [ ] Hit rate dashboard
- [ ] Model improvement: wrong predictions → recalibrate

## Phase 7: Dashboard (Paid Tier)

- [ ] React + Vite dashboard
- [ ] Project list with completeness scores
- [ ] Spec editor with live validation
- [ ] Prediction tracker with hit rate charts
- [ ] Team management
